title: An October Surprise
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: pres_year = 1 and month = 10 and october_done != year and (dissent_percent >= 10 or maga_strength >= 30)
priority: 260

= An October Surprise

Days before the election, a damaging story about our campaign breaks, whether it is an investigation, a leak, or a hacked email trove. The media amplifies it. Our opponents seize on it.

- @surprise_transparent: Release everything
- @surprise_counter: Counterattack
- @surprise_silence: Ignore it and keep campaigning

@surprise_transparent
on-arrival: october_done = year; dem_enthusiasm -= 0.3; pro_democracy += 0.5; suburban_dem += 1*(1-dissent); resources -= 0

We insist on full transparency. The story fades, though not before it hurts.

@surprise_counter
on-arrival: october_done = year; polarization += 1; dem_enthusiasm += 0.3; suburban_dem -= 2*(1-dissent); gop_enthusiasm += 0.3

We attack the sources and the motive. The story drags on.

@surprise_silence
on-arrival: october_done = year; suburban_dem -= 3*(1-dissent); dem_enthusiasm -= 0.5; working_dem -= 1*(1-dissent)

We say nothing. The story grows in the vacuum.
